# The killer analogy is build systems

Imagine if every time one file changed, `cargo` did:

```text
DELETE EVERYTHING
COMPILE THE ENTIRE WORLD AGAIN
```

We solved that decades ago with dependency graphs.

Agents are currently doing the epistemic equivalent.

```text
1000 conclusions
       │
source changes
       │
       ├── naive approach
       │      ↓
       │   rerun 1000
       │
       └── Aletheia
              ↓
        find dependency cut
              ↓
         rerun affected 47
```

**Aletheia is incremental build infrastructure for derived knowledge.**

That is vastly more exciting than “freshness receipts.”

And unlike the current arbitrary `47/1000` example in `pitch-highsignal.md`, we should benchmark this properly before attaching percentages. The existing repo itself admits that the 58% avoided-work figure came from a comparison whose query scopes did not overlap cleanly.

