# This unlocks persistent autonomous agents

This should probably be your primary future slide.

OpenAIRE explicitly says their agents should move beyond search into literature reviews, citation analysis, author/career mapping, dataset assessment, bibliometric intelligence and cross-domain synthesis. ([OpenAIRE][5]) OpenAIRE describes the integration as a foundation for how science is accessed, funded and performed in an AI era. ([OpenAIRE Innovation][6])

Alien already persists agent conversations through LangGraph/PostgreSQL and is running internal research agents against its OpenAIRE bibliometric MCP. ([Alien Club][2])

Once agents persist, this becomes inevitable:

```text
Day 1
Agent learns X

Day 8
Agent builds Y using X

Day 40
Agent recommends Z because of Y

Day 91
Source underlying X changes
```

A normal memory store knows:

```text
X exists
```

Aletheia knows:

```text
X was justified by A+B

A changed

therefore:
X → recheck
Y → potentially affected
Z → potentially affected
```

That's **dependency-aware long-term agent memory**.

Much more compelling.

