# And yes: it enables smarter model routing

This is where the economic story gets really strong.

Aletheia produces a **proof obligation**.

That obligation tells you what has to be established.

So you can route the cheapest possible computation capable of satisfying it:

```text
Proof obligation
      │
      ▼
Can deterministic code resolve it?
      │
 YES ─┘ → $≈0

 NO
      ↓
Can cheap model resolve it?
      │
 YES ─┘ → cheap inference

 NO
      ↓
frontier model

still uncertain?
      ↓
human expert
```

This is much better than:

```text
Claude everywhere
```

It becomes:

> **Verification-aware compute routing.**

Or even better:

> **Spend intelligence proportional to epistemic risk.**

Alien already intentionally abstracts across Claude, GPT, Mistral and Gemini rather than hard-wiring one model. ([Alien Club][2])

Aletheia could eventually determine **which model deserves which task**, based on:

```text
blast radius
claim importance
verification difficulty
uncertainty
recomputability
source health
```

That gives the long-term architecture:

```text
              ALETHEIA
                 │
       what must be re-established?
                 │
                 ▼
          proof obligation
                 │
          risk / crux score
                 │
       ┌─────────┼─────────┐
       ▼         ▼         ▼
 deterministic cheap      frontier
    code        model      model
       │         │         │
       └─────────┼─────────┘
                 ▼
              VERIFY
                 │
                 ▼
        Freshness Receipt
```

Now we're talking about a serious autonomous-agent control plane.

