# You can even derive the economic equation

The core value proposition becomes:

[
\text{Savings}
==============

## C_{\text{full rerun}}

\left(
C_{\text{change detection}}
+
C_{\text{affected recomputation}}
\right)
]

Or per maintenance cycle:

```text
Full recomputation:

C_full = Σ all derivations C(d)


Aletheia:

C_incremental =
    C_dependency_check
    +
    Σ affected derivations C(d)
```

So:

```text
Savings ratio =
1 - C_incremental / C_full
```

And at scale:

```text
Annual maintenance cost =
number of stored derived objects
× upstream change frequency
× average derivation cost
```

Aletheia attacks the multiplication by replacing:

```text
all stored objects
```

with:

```text
affected objects
```

That's the economic argument.

