# There is also a reliability payoff

Money isn't even the whole story.

Rerunning an LLM is **not equivalent to maintaining an existing derivation**.

You might get:

```text
T1:
Claim C = supported

T2:
same source data
same question
different sampling/model
→ Claim C = unsupported
```

So “just rerun it” introduces unnecessary nondeterminism.

Aletheia allows:

```text
nothing material changed
        ↓
reuse established result
```

That is better engineering.

You only reopen a conclusion **when its premises require it**.

